-- title:
--   Injective archimedean local bridge at an infinite place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a representation $M$ of $G_{\mathbb Q}=\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ over $\mathbb Z/p$. Let $F\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field which is a number field, Galois over $\mathbb Q$ and totally complex, let $w$ be an infinite place of $F$, and write $D_w=\mathrm{decomp}\;\mathbb Q\;F\;w$ for the stabiliser of $w$ in $\operatorname{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$. Let $\sigma\in G_{\mathbb Q}$ and let $\pi_i$ be a homomorphism from $\mathrm{archimedeanDecomposition}$, the subgroup of $G_{\mathbb Q}$ generated by $\mathrm{complexConjugation}$, to $D_w$, such that each $\pi_i(h)$, viewed in $\operatorname{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$, is the restriction to $F$ of $\sigma^{-1}h\sigma$; assume $\pi_i$ is bijective and that $\sigma^{-1}\,\mathrm{complexConjugation}\,\sigma$ does not lie in the fixing subgroup of $F$. Let $R\xrightarrow{f}P\xrightarrow{g}B$ be $\mathbb Z[\operatorname{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)]$-module maps with $f$ injective, the pair exact and $g$ surjective, with $P$ isomorphic to the free representation on a finite type $\alpha$ and $pB=0$. Let $\kappa:B\to\operatorname{Hom}(M,\mathrm{Additive}\,(F_w)^\times)$ be biadditive, equivariant in the sense $\kappa(\rho_B(\pi_i h)b,\rho_M(h)m)=\rho(\pi_i h)\kappa(b,m)$ for the action of $D_w$ on $(F_w)^\times$, and perfect in the sense that every additive map $B\to\mathrm{Additive}\,(F_w)^\times$ is $\kappa(\cdot,m)$ for a unique $m\in M$. Then there is an additive homomorphism $\Lambda$ from $H^1\bigl(D_w,\operatorname{Hom}(R,(F_w)^\times)\bigr)$, the internal hom of the restriction of $R$ to $D_w$ with $\mathrm{localUnits}$, to the continuous $H^2$ of $\mathrm{archimedeanDecomposition}$ with coefficients in $M$ restricted along $\mathrm{archimedeanLoc}$, such that the predicate `IsLocalBridge₂` holds for $\mathrm{archimedeanLoc}$, $\pi_i$, the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $D_w$, the coefficient module $\mathrm{localUnits}$ pulled back along $\pi_i$ with the identity comparison map on $\mathrm{Additive}\,(F_w)^\times$, $\kappa$ and $\Lambda$, and moreover $\Lambda$ is injective.
--
--   This is the archimedean local term in degree two of the Tate-duality bookkeeping: it identifies the relation-module presentation of $\operatorname{Ext}^2_{D_w}(B,(F_w)^\times)$ with continuous $H^2$ of the decomposition group at an infinite place acting on $M$, injectively. It is used on the $Ш^2$ side of the Šafarevič–Tate pairing, in [`groupCohomology.exists_sha1_dualTwist_sha2_pairing_nondegenerate_of_ne_two`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_sha1_dualTwist_sha2_pairing_nondegenerate_of_ne_two).
